A||||2||fiero56||roastin' 'em||||14
Z||000000||fiero56||10-15-1999||11:44 PM||||So there I was, waiting at a stop-light in my own little world, trying to figure out where that valve noise is coming from(on tech list).  I rev the engine a couple times to see if the noise changes.  That's when I heard it.  From beside me comes this very low and loud rumble.  I look over, and I couldn't believe it, I had been so tuned into my car that I didn't see the car next to me.  There sat a guy in his newer black Viper giving me the nod. I think "yeah right, I'm in a Fiero, he's in a Viper".  I declined.  I just eased her along while he roasted em and gave everyone around a nice "smoke show".  Was a beautiful site.  Wish mine could do that.  I just had to ramble....||||reg||14
Z||000001||87FieroGT||10-16-1999||01:24 AM||||You need to make yourself a V8 Fiero. Then you might have a chance.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mwbackus||10-16-1999||03:46 AM||||According to my calculations, a Fiero with a 400hp V8 will be in "front" of a stock Viper at the end of the quarter mile.  A "Brand New" ZZ-4 350 V8 from GM Performance can be obtained with this kind of power for around $5k.  I am sure that additional costs beyond that of a swap kit would be required to transmit this power efficiently and safely to the ground.  Still, I would say that someone with the required capabilities could convert a Fiero into a Viper killer for under $10k. <P>Mike||||reg||1
